-> The same domain-materialization `∪`/`∩` get (see
-> set_op_domain_materialize.code) applies to Schema and Union domains too,
-> not just scalar number ranges — a variable's domain can be "any kind".

-> Schema domain: p ∈ K where K's only field has a finite domain — p's
-> domain enumerates as the Cartesian product of its fields (here, one
-> field, two values).
K = { x ∈ {1, 2} }
p ∈ K
extra = { "z" }
c = extra ∪ p
assert c = { "z", { x = 1 }, { x = 2 } }

-> Union domain: s ∈ Status, where Status mixes a bare value and a schema.
-> Enumerating concatenates each alternative's own finite candidates.
Status = {"Success"} ∪ { code ∈ {1, 2} }
s ∈ Status
d = extra ∪ s
assert d = { "z", "Success", { code = 1 }, { code = 2 } }

-> The same finite_candidates() engine backs `loop <var> { }` (T26 Phase
-> 1) — a Schema domain is now loopable too, for free.
loop p get pts {
    yield p
}
assert pts = [{ x = 1 }, { x = 2 }]
